	(1975, 1110, 'pubs ext vt edu 422 422 023 422 023 html', 'https://www.pubs.ext.vt.edu/422/422-023/422-023.html', NULL, '**Fruit Growers Calendar:** Fruit Production is a Year-Round Activity || | Month | Activity | || | May | * Install rodent guards around trunk of newly planted trees. * Thin fruit with chemicals or by hand. * Apply petal fall and first cover spray. * Remove fireblight strikes. * Discourage deer...'),
	(1976, 1100, 'Arseneault 2016 A review of apple preharvest fruit drop and p', 'https://doi.org/10.1016/j.scienta.2016.08.002', NULL, 'Furthermore, foliar boron sprays applied during rapid fruit growth on the two || cultivars ‘Fuji’ and ‘Orin’ improved fruit soluble sugars and starch at three orchards (Lu et al., 2013).'),
	(1977, 1100, 'Penn State Tree Fruit Produc', '/api/kb/assets/pdf/e5ae1a65affc1a1b/Penn_State_Tree_Fruit_Produc.pdf#page=27', 'p. 27', 'Boron is most effective when applied as a foliar spray on apples and to a lesser extent on pears. || Foliar applications can be made during bloom or postharvest while leaves are still green and active on the tree.'),
	(1978, 1100, 'tree fruit horticulture vaes vt edu 2025 04 05 pre bloom bloom nutrition and growth management for apple orcha', 'https://tree-fruit-horticulture.vaes.vt.edu/2025/04/05/pre-bloom-bloom-nutrition-and-growth-management-for-apple-orchards/', NULL, 'Calcium uptake is critical in the early weeks after bloom, especially for sensitive varieties like Honeycrisp. || Begin foliar calcium applications at pink or early bloom, and continue through the early cover sprays.'),
	(1979, 1093, 'Apples   Botany, Production and Uses   D. Ferree, I. Warrington (CABI, 2003) BBS', '/api/kb/assets/pdf/435dfba709ef04c7/Apples%20-%20Botany%2C%20Production%20and%20Uses%20-%20D.%20Ferree%2C%20I.%20Warrington%20%28CABI%2C%202003%29%20BBS.pdf#page=90', 'p. 90, 91, 341', 'These strains reportedly differ from the standard in fruit size, flesh colour (whiter), tree spurriness or compactness, ripening time, fruit set, internode length, lenticel prominence, productivity and the presence of dark green stripes in ''Granspur'' (Brooks and Olmo, 1997). Most plantings are...'),
	(1980, 1093, 'extension umd edu resource important apple cultivars mid atlantic region eb 2023 0684', 'https://extension.umd.edu/resource/important-apple-cultivars-mid-atlantic-region-eb-2023-0684', NULL, 'It is of paramount importance to conduct a trial planting with a small number of trees before embarking on large-scale plantings of a new cultivar. This preliminary step ensures that the cultivars not only meet production and target market requirements but also thrive in the specific...'),
	(1981, 1093, 'niab com number trees pollinating variety planted relation numbers main variety', 'https://www.niab.com/number-trees-pollinating-variety-planted-relation-numbers-main-variety', NULL, 'Another consideration is the maximum distance between the pollinating variety and the main variety. There is evidence to suggest that distances above 15 to 20 m are likely to result in reduced pollination efficiency ([Mišić, 1994; Free and Spencer-Botth, 1964](/node/1827)).'),
	(2000, 1081, 'Kumawat 2021 Tall Spindle Apple orchard planting system f', '/api/kb/assets/pdf/f9c53384f34ce57e/Kumawat_2021_Tall-Spindle-Apple-orchard-planting-system-f.pdf', NULL, 'This can be achieved by annual removal of large one or two upper branches completely by “bevel cut” so that small stub of the lower portion of branch remains which often result in flat, weak replacement branch. When such type of pruning is repeated annually, the top of the tree can be composed...'),
	(1982, 1068, 'agriculture canada ca en agricultural production crop protection agricultural pest management resources apple', 'https://agriculture.canada.ca/en/agricultural-production/crop-protection/agricultural-pest-management-resources/apple-scab-improving-understanding-better-management', NULL, 'A **pre-infection** fungicide is applied before an infection period begins, and protects the leaves and fruits from becoming infected. The product will be effective only on the leaves or fruits present when the trees are sprayed. The active ingredient prevents the first stages of fungus...'),
	(1983, 1068, 'niab com chemical control apple canker', 'https://www.niab.com/chemical-control-apple-canker', NULL, 'The recent inoculation studies indicate a slight increase in fruit susceptibility to *Neonectria ditissima* pre-harvest, but it is not known whether there is any benefit from additional sprays at this time and there is the risk of fungicide residues in fruit from the late applications.'),
	(1984, 1068, 'pubs ext vt edu SPES spes 755 html', 'https://pubs.ext.vt.edu/SPES/spes-755.html', NULL, 'European canker remains one of the most significant challenges in apple production. Its complex disease cycle, long infection latency, and adaptability make it difficult to control, particularly in humid climates where environmental conditions favor infection (e.g., Canada, United Kingdom, New...'),
	(1985, 1086, 'bctfpg ca horticulture fruit tree nutrition essential mineral nutrients in plants deficiency toxicity symptoms', 'https://www.bctfpg.ca/horticulture/fruit-tree-nutrition/essential-mineral-nutrients-in-plants-deficiency-toxicity-symptoms-sources-recommendations/boron-b/', NULL, 'Leaves showing suspicious symptoms can be collected in May for analysis to compare to regular leaf analysis done in July. Leaf analysis cannot be used to test B levels after post-bloom sprays have been applied to foliage. To avoid this problem, B can be applied effectively in the fall before...'),
	(1986, 1086, 'fruit wisc edu 2020 04 28 managing micronutrients in apple orchards prebloom foliar applications', 'https://fruit.wisc.edu/2020/04/28/managing-micronutrients-in-apple-orchards-prebloom-foliar-applications/', NULL, 'In an orchard without boron deficiency, 2 lbs of boron/ac uniformly broadcast or sprayed over the soil (this can be done during spring, summer, or fall), plus a foliar spray of Solubor at 1 lb per 100 gallons dilute during tight cluster to pink are recommended.'),
	(1987, 1086, 'tree fruit horticulture vaes vt edu 2025 04 05 pre bloom bloom nutrition and growth management for apple orcha', 'https://tree-fruit-horticulture.vaes.vt.edu/2025/04/05/pre-bloom-bloom-nutrition-and-growth-management-for-apple-orchards/', NULL, 'Calcium uptake is critical in the early weeks after bloom, especially for sensitive varieties like Honeycrisp. || Begin foliar calcium applications at pink or early bloom, and continue through the early cover sprays.'),
	(1988, 1065, 'web archive org web 19981207060318id http www caf wvu edu kearneysville disease descriptions omblight html', 'https://web.archive.org/web/19981207060318id_/http://www.caf.wvu.edu/kearneysville/disease_descriptions/omblight.html', NULL, 'Although mature shoot and limb || tissues are generally resistant to infection by E. amylovora, injuries caused by hail, || late frosts of 28 F (-2 C) or lower, and high winds that damage the foliage can create a || trauma blight situation in which the normal defense mechanisms in mature tissues...'),
	(1989, 1065, 'Penn State Tree Fruit Produc', '/api/kb/assets/pdf/e5ae1a65affc1a1b/Penn_State_Tree_Fruit_Produc.pdf#page=119', 'p. 119, 120, 126', 'Phytophthora collar, crown, and root rots continue to be a major cause of tree death in Pennsylvania orchards. These rots can affect both pome and stone fruit. || The fungus can infect apple trees in the following ways: (1) collar rot, infection above the tree union; (2) crown rot, infection of...'),
	(1990, 1063, 'niab com flower blossom thinning', 'https://www.niab.com/flower-blossom-thinning', NULL, 'Other blossom thinners that have shown promise in trials both in the UK and abroad include [Armothin](/node/1899), common [salt (sodium chloride)](/node/1904), [Endothallic acid](/node/1896), [Ethephon](/node/1900), Lime sulphur, [Pelargonic acid](/node/1897), [Urea](/node/1901),...'),
	(1991, 1063, 'Peck 2006 Apple Orchard Productivity and Fruit Quality', 'https://doi.org/10.21273/hortsci.41.1.99', NULL, NULL),
	(1992, 1063, 'bctfpg ca horticulture spray thinning growth regulators sun burn protection', 'https://www.bctfpg.ca/horticulture/spray-thinning-growth-regulators-sun-burn-protection/', NULL, 'Accede is a new plant growth regulator that is now registered for apple thinning in Canada. Its active ingredient is a naturally occurring compound, 1-Aminocyclopropane- 1-carboxyllic acid (ACC), the precursor to ethylene synthesis in all plants. Applying Accede when king fruitlets are at the...'),
	(1993, 1084, 'AP12029 final report', '/api/kb/assets/pdf/539bd5109d6b5bd4/AP12029-final-report.pdf#page=63', 'p. 63, 64, 65', 'This consistent shift in timing was associated with an unusual autumn and winter chill accumulation pattern (Figure 7). Total chill accumulated up to 31 August was similar in 2013 and 2014, 73 and 75 chill portions respectively. However, in 2014 there was a warm week in late-May to early-June...'),
	(1994, 1084, 'A3560', '/api/kb/assets/pdf/45bab9435ab5a493/A3560.pdf#page=5', 'p. 5', 'W isconsin''s cold climate presents problems for keeping trees alive during the winter. Two types of winter injury are common in || Wisconsin. The first type of damage is caused when the trunk warms from sunlight reflected off snow. As the trunk tissues warm, the cells become active and lose...'),
	(1995, 1084, 'Apples   Botany, Production and Uses   D. Ferree, I. Warrington (CABI, 2003) BBS', '/api/kb/assets/pdf/435dfba709ef04c7/Apples%20-%20Botany%2C%20Production%20and%20Uses%20-%20D.%20Ferree%2C%20I.%20Warrington%20%28CABI%2C%202003%29%20BBS.pdf', NULL, 'The dew-point is important in the rate of temperature fall. At the dew-point, energy from the heat of condensation (stored or latent heat) is released. This heat, when added to the atmosphere, decreases the rate of temperature fall significantly. Above the dew-point, temperature fall is...'),
	(1996, 1104, 'extension umaine edu fruit growing fruit trees in maine spraying', 'https://extension.umaine.edu/fruit/growing-fruit-trees-in-maine/spraying/', NULL, '| 16 | 1.4 gallons | 1.9 gallons | 2.7 gallons | || | **Tree height and width (feet)** | Volume of water | | | || | *Bud break* | *Mid-season* | *Late-season* |'),
	(1997, 1077, 'postharvest hortgro co za pag south african controlled atmosphere storage operators manual', 'https://postharvest.hortgro.co.za/pag/south-african-controlled-atmosphere-storage-operators-manual/', NULL, 'Reduction of the spore load must begin in the orchard before harvest. Decayed fruit and pruning, which provides nutrients for fungi, must be removed. Fungal spores produced by fungi on dead twigs or decayed fruit on the orchard floor spread to fruit on the tree or to adjacent roads. When fruit...'),
	(1998, 1077, 'CommercialStorage', '/api/kb/assets/pdf/98fe86ba0a133c7d/CommercialStorage.pdf#page=201', 'p. 201', 'Many of the biocontrol agents selected and developed to date have proven very effective in controlled tests, but commercialization of biocontrols has been slow. Product developers view the market potential for postharvest treatments as relatively limited because the products are applied in a...'),
	(1999, 1077, 'postharvest hortgro co za pag best practice guidelines fuji 2023', 'https://postharvest.hortgro.co.za/pag/best-practice-guidelines_fuji_2023/', NULL, 'Drench with Fludioxonil or Pyrimethanil (Fludioxonil preferred)'),
