	(2032, 1078, 'Penn State Tree Fruit Produc', '/api/kb/assets/pdf/e5ae1a65affc1a1b/Penn_State_Tree_Fruit_Produc.pdf#page=17', 'p. 17', 'Herbicides must (1) adequately contact the target weeds, (2) be absorbed by the weed, (3) move within the weed to the site of action without being neutralized, and (4) be in high enough concentration to be toxic at the site of action. The mode of action refers to the chain of events from...'),
	(2033, 1078, 'pubs ext vt edu 422 422 023 422 023 html', 'https://www.pubs.ext.vt.edu/422/422-023/422-023.html', NULL, '**Fruit Growers Calendar:** Fruit Production is a Year-Round Activity || | Month | Activity | || | April | * Apply dormant oil spray, green tip, prepink, and pink sprays for insects and diseases. * Measures to control weeds should begin early |'),
	(2034, 1078, '2023 2024 New Jersey Commercial Tree Fruit Production Guide', '/api/kb/assets/pdf/5769fc173448184d/2023_2024%20New%20Jersey%20Commercial%20Tree%20Fruit%20Production%20Guide.pdf', NULL, NULL),
	(2035, 1080, 'A3560', 'https://hort.extension.wisc.edu/files/2020/02/A3560.pdf', NULL, 'Pollinizers. Most apples are self-unfruitful. That means that pollen from a given cultivar will not pollinate itself (won''t produce viable seed). Some apples are partially self-fruitful but will produce larger crops if cross pollination is provided. As a general rule, apples should not be...'),
	(2036, 1080, 'extension psu edu orchard pollination pollinizers pollinators and weather', 'https://extension.psu.edu/orchard-pollination-pollinizers-pollinators-and-weather', NULL, 'The EPP was introduced in the mid-1960s to establish the time frame between when a flower is pollinated and when the embryo becomes unreceptive. After pollination, the pollen tube takes a certain time to reach the embryo sac. Once a flower opens, the embryo has only a limited time when it is...'),
	(2037, 1080, 'pubs ext vt edu 422 422 023 422 023 html', 'https://www.pubs.ext.vt.edu/422/422-023/422-023.html', NULL, 'Triploid varieties such as ‘Winesap’, ‘Jona- gold’, ‘Mutsu’, and ‘Stayman’ have three sets of chromosomes, produce nonviable pollen, and are not effective pollenizers.'),
	(2038, 1094, 'tree fruit horticulture vaes vt edu 2025 04 05 pre bloom bloom nutrition and growth management for apple orcha', 'https://tree-fruit-horticulture.vaes.vt.edu/2025/04/05/pre-bloom-bloom-nutrition-and-growth-management-for-apple-orchards/', NULL, 'Calcium uptake is critical in the early weeks after bloom, especially for sensitive varieties like Honeycrisp. || Begin foliar calcium applications at pink or early bloom, and continue through the early cover sprays.'),
	(2039, 1094, 'bctfpg ca horticulture fruit tree nutrition essential mineral nutrients in plants deficiency toxicity symptoms', 'https://www.bctfpg.ca/horticulture/fruit-tree-nutrition/essential-mineral-nutrients-in-plants-deficiency-toxicity-symptoms-sources-recommendations/nitrogen-n/', NULL, 'Table 6. Timing and rates of foliar urea (46-0-0) spray for fruit trees || | Type of tree | Time of application | Rate of application (Airblast sprayer – Dilute) | || | Per ha | Per acre | Per 100 L | || | Young non-bearing trees with poor growth - 2 sprays 2 weeks apart. | June - July | 11 kg |...'),
	(2040, 1094, 'bctfpg ca horticulture fruit tree nutrition essential mineral nutrients in plants deficiency toxicity symptoms', 'https://www.bctfpg.ca/horticulture/fruit-tree-nutrition/essential-mineral-nutrients-in-plants-deficiency-toxicity-symptoms-sources-recommendations/magnesium-mg/', NULL, 'Table 1. Possible magnesium foliar application rates. || | **Type of Treatment** | **Frequency of Application** | **Type of Material** | **Rate of Application** | || | Curative spray | Repeat preventative spray two or three times, at 2-3 week intervals depending on the severity of the deficiency. |'),
	(2041, 1091, 'bctfpg ca horticulture fruit tree nutrition essential mineral nutrients in plants deficiency toxicity symptoms', 'https://www.bctfpg.ca/horticulture/fruit-tree-nutrition/essential-mineral-nutrients-in-plants-deficiency-toxicity-symptoms-sources-recommendations/nitrogen-n/', NULL, 'Table 6. Timing and rates of foliar urea (46-0-0) spray for fruit trees || | Type of tree | Time of application | Rate of application (Airblast sprayer – Dilute) | || | Per ha | Per acre | Per 100 L | || | Young non-bearing trees with poor growth - 2 sprays 2 weeks apart. | June - July | 11 kg |...'),
	(2042, 1091, 'postharvest hortgro co za pag south african controlled atmosphere storage operators manual', 'https://postharvest.hortgro.co.za/pag/south-african-controlled-atmosphere-storage-operators-manual/', NULL, 'Fruitlet analysis samples on apples are conducted around 62 days DAFB. These results can be used to determine the number of calcium sprays per orchard. Granny Smith which is not as susceptible to bitter pit and which has a long storage life, is usually given six calcium sprays whereas Golden...'),
	(2043, 1091, 'Penn State Tree Fruit Produc', '/api/kb/assets/pdf/e5ae1a65affc1a1b/Penn_State_Tree_Fruit_Produc.pdf#page=27', 'p. 27', 'Boron is most effective when applied as a foliar spray on apples and to a lesser extent on pears. || Foliar applications can be made during bloom or postharvest while leaves are still green and active on the tree.'),
	(2044, 1111, 'web archive org web 19990117024948id http www caf wvu edu kearneysville disease descriptions omblackr html', 'https://web.archive.org/web/19990117024948id_/http://www.caf.wvu.edu/kearneysville/disease_descriptions/omblackr.html', NULL, 'The margin of the lesions remains purple, while the center turns tan to brown. In a few weeks, > > secondary enlargement of these leaf spots occurs. At this time, the lesions assume a > > characteristic "frog-eye" appearance (photo 2-30). As they age, a series of > > concentric rings develops...'),
	(2045, 1111, 'agriculture canada ca en agricultural production crop protection agricultural pest management resources resist', 'https://agriculture.canada.ca/en/agricultural-production/crop-protection/agricultural-pest-management-resources/resistance-apple-scab-pathogen-fungicides-canadian-orchards-knowing-and-managing-risk', NULL, 'Initial infections lead to production of spores which can cause multiple secondary infections during the season. Wind and moisture are necessary for spore discharge and germination as well as for subsequent infection of apple tissue. With frequent rainfall, the control of apple scab becomes...'),
	(2046, 1111, 'Penn State Tree Fruit Produc', '/api/kb/assets/pdf/e5ae1a65affc1a1b/Penn_State_Tree_Fruit_Produc.pdf#page=119', 'p. 119, 120, 126', 'Phytophthora collar, crown, and root rots continue to be a major cause of tree death in Pennsylvania orchards. These rots can affect both pome and stone fruit. || The fungus can infect apple trees in the following ways: (1) collar rot, infection above the tree union; (2) crown rot, infection of...'),
	(2047, 1059, 'pubs ext vt edu content pubs ext vt edu en 422 422 023 422 023 html', 'https://www.pubs.ext.vt.edu/content/pubs_ext_vt_edu/en/422/422-023/422-023.html', NULL, '| Petal fall - flower petals fall from the blossom | white apple leaf hopper, spotted tentiform leafhopper, plum curculio, green fruit worms, plant bugs, aphids, leaf rollers, codling moth, apple scab, rusts, powdery mildew, rots |'),
	(2048, 1059, 'extension uconn edu publication ipm plan san jose scale', 'https://extension.uconn.edu/publication/ipm-plan-san-jose-scale', NULL, 'A dormant or delayed dormant oil application can be applied before pink bud stage to reduce overwintering populations.'),
	(2049, 1059, 'pubs ext vt edu 422 422 023 422 023 html', 'https://www.pubs.ext.vt.edu/422/422-023/422-023.html', NULL, '**Fruit Growers Calendar:** Fruit Production is a Year-Round Activity || | Month | Activity | || | May | * Install rodent guards around trunk of newly planted trees. * Thin fruit with chemicals or by hand. * Apply petal fall and first cover spray. * Remove fireblight strikes. * Discourage deer...'),
	(2050, 1108, 'extension psu edu orchard pollination pollinizers pollinators and weather', 'https://extension.psu.edu/orchard-pollination-pollinizers-pollinators-and-weather', NULL, 'The EPP was introduced in the mid-1960s to establish the time frame between when a flower is pollinated and when the embryo becomes unreceptive. After pollination, the pollen tube takes a certain time to reach the embryo sac. Once a flower opens, the embryo has only a limited time when it is...'),
	(2051, 1108, 'hortgro co za news pollination in the spotlight', 'https://www.hortgro.co.za/news/pollination-in-the-spotlight/', NULL, 'Protective netting can also complicate pollination. In some fixed or fully enclosed net structures, bees can become disorientated or have difficulty navigating between the orchard and their hives, potentially reducing pollination efficiency. The effect will depend on the design and size of the...'),
	(2052, 1108, 'bctfpg ca horticulture varieties and pollination', 'https://www.bctfpg.ca/horticulture/varieties-and-pollination/', NULL, 'Pollination is a critical but very brief event in the production cycle of all tree fruits, **including self-fertile varieties**. Good conditions for pollination may exist for only a few hours during bloom. Because of its importance, pollination should be planned and not left to chance.'),
	(2053, 1055, 'niab com suitable pollinating varieties', 'https://www.niab.com/suitable-pollinating-varieties', NULL, 'Even in apparently incompatible combinations fruit set is often able to occur. * For instance, trials have shown that when Fiesta received pollen of another variety, with which it should be incompatible, it was able to set a reasonable crop of fruits. * However, when the reciprocal cross was...'),
	(2054, 1055, 'Apples   Botany, Production and Uses   D. Ferree, I. Warrington (CABI, 2003) BBS', '/api/kb/assets/pdf/435dfba709ef04c7/Apples%20-%20Botany%2C%20Production%20and%20Uses%20-%20D.%20Ferree%2C%20I.%20Warrington%20%28CABI%2C%202003%29%20BBS.pdf#page=90', 'p. 90, 91, 341', 'These strains reportedly differ from the standard in fruit size, flesh colour (whiter), tree spurriness or compactness, ripening time, fruit set, internode length, lenticel prominence, productivity and the presence of dark green stripes in ''Granspur'' (Brooks and Olmo, 1997). Most plantings are...'),
	(2055, 1055, 'niab com management pollinating variety orchard', 'https://www.niab.com/management-pollinating-variety-orchard', NULL, 'If pollinating varieties, either standard fruit varieties or ornamental *Malus*, are to flower consistently, abundantly and produce good pollen, it is essential that they are well-managed within the main orchard.'),
	(2056, 1098, 'bctfpg ca horticulture spray thinning growth regulators sun burn protection', 'https://www.bctfpg.ca/horticulture/spray-thinning-growth-regulators-sun-burn-protection/', NULL, 'Accede is a new plant growth regulator that is now registered for apple thinning in Canada. Its active ingredient is a naturally occurring compound, 1-Aminocyclopropane- 1-carboxyllic acid (ACC), the precursor to ethylene synthesis in all plants. Applying Accede when king fruitlets are at the...'),
	(2057, 1098, 'Apples   Botany, Production and Uses   D. Ferree, I. Warrington (CABI, 2003) BBS', '/api/kb/assets/pdf/435dfba709ef04c7/Apples%20-%20Botany%2C%20Production%20and%20Uses%20-%20D.%20Ferree%2C%20I.%20Warrington%20%28CABI%2C%202003%29%20BBS.pdf#page=491', 'p. 491', '''Jonathan'' can produce parthenocarpic fruit after GA application (Thomas, 1963). Early thinning is required; it has a slight tendency to biennial bearing. If trees are biennial or too vigorous, root pruning in combination with supplemental irrigation is a useful tool (Ferre, 1992). Ethephon,...'),
	(2058, 1098, 'blogs cornell edu enychp tree fruit apples 2025 capital region petal fall thinning meeting summary', 'https://blogs.cornell.edu/enychp/tree-fruit/apples/2025-capital-region-petal-fall-thinning-meeting-summary', NULL, '- 100ppm (64 oz) Maxcel per 100 gallons dilute TRV + 1pt Sevin/100 for Gala, Snapdragon, and Empire || **Rate recommendations for this timing:** || To double check your window, enter your full bloom dates into the [apple carbohydrate model](https://newa.cornell.edu/apple-carbohydrate-thinning/).'),
	(2059, 1075, 'CA Manual Revised', '/api/kb/assets/pdf/dac8958cf8856eca/CA-Manual-Revised.pdf#page=82', 'p. 82, 83, 84', 'Small, brown lesions rapidly increase in size and the fruit is completely decayed within two days. The skin of a decayed fruit has a parchment-like texture and does not break easily. Decayed tissue is very watery. Spores are produced at skin breaks and at the stem and calyx ends of the affected...'),
	(2060, 1075, 'CommercialStorage', '/api/kb/assets/pdf/98fe86ba0a133c7d/CommercialStorage.pdf#page=201', 'p. 201', 'Many of the biocontrol agents selected and developed to date have proven very effective in controlled tests, but commercialization of biocontrols has been slow. Product developers view the market potential for postharvest treatments as relatively limited because the products are applied in a...'),
	(2061, 1075, 'Penn State Tree Fruit Produc', '/api/kb/assets/pdf/e5ae1a65affc1a1b/Penn_State_Tree_Fruit_Produc.pdf#page=119', 'p. 119, 120, 126', 'Phytophthora collar, crown, and root rots continue to be a major cause of tree death in Pennsylvania orchards. These rots can affect both pome and stone fruit. || The fungus can infect apple trees in the following ways: (1) collar rot, infection above the tree union; (2) crown rot, infection of...'),
	(2062, 1089, 'bctfpg ca horticulture fruit tree nutrition essential mineral nutrients in plants deficiency toxicity symptoms', 'https://www.bctfpg.ca/horticulture/fruit-tree-nutrition/essential-mineral-nutrients-in-plants-deficiency-toxicity-symptoms-sources-recommendations/boron-b/', NULL, 'Leaves showing suspicious symptoms can be collected in May for analysis to compare to regular leaf analysis done in July. Leaf analysis cannot be used to test B levels after post-bloom sprays have been applied to foliage. To avoid this problem, B can be applied effectively in the fall before...'),
	(2063, 1089, 'bctfpg ca horticulture fruit tree nutrition essential mineral nutrients in plants deficiency toxicity symptoms', 'https://www.bctfpg.ca/horticulture/fruit-tree-nutrition/essential-mineral-nutrients-in-plants-deficiency-toxicity-symptoms-sources-recommendations/zinc-zn/', NULL, 'For apples, it is recommended that Zn sulphate be applied annually at silver tip to green tip stage of bud development (stages 2 and 3), supplemented by one or more sprays of chelated foliar formulations of Zn during the growing season.'),
	(2064, 1089, 'tree fruit horticulture vaes vt edu 2025 04 05 pre bloom bloom nutrition and growth management for apple orcha', 'https://tree-fruit-horticulture.vaes.vt.edu/2025/04/05/pre-bloom-bloom-nutrition-and-growth-management-for-apple-orchards/', NULL, 'Calcium uptake is critical in the early weeks after bloom, especially for sensitive varieties like Honeycrisp. || Begin foliar calcium applications at pink or early bloom, and continue through the early cover sprays.'),
	(2065, 1072, 'lof cce cornell edu submission php id 170', 'https://lof.cce.cornell.edu/submission.php?id=170', NULL, 'In recent years, fall planting has become the norm for a few Western NY growers who have successfully planted in the fall for several consecutive years. These new orchards have shown a strong growth the first year compared to spring planted trees.'),
	(2066, 1072, 'The Tall Spindle Planting System 2746zv0', 'https://blogs.cornell.edu/newfruit/files/2016/12/The-Tall-Spindle-Planting-System-2746zv0.pdf#page=1', 'p. 1, 2', 'The Tall Spindle planting system is a planting system particularly suited for New York. It maximizes profitability through early yield, improved fruit quality, reduced spraying, pruning, and training costs, and the ability to rapidly turn over apple varieties from those less profitable to those...'),
	(2067, 1116, 'treefruit wsu edu article recommended harvest criteria for commercial wa 38 storage in 2026', 'https://treefruit.wsu.edu/article/recommended-harvest-criteria-for-commercial-wa-38-storage-in-2026/', NULL, 'Heavy cropping of 2 year-old trees may stunt tree growth and/or induce biennial bearing. || Commercial WA 38 harvest recommendations for storage'),
	(2102, 1074, '2020 21 australian apple and pear ipdm manual', '/api/kb/assets/pdf/44a02a4cb9e3415a/2020-21-australian-apple-and-pear-ipdm-manual.pdf#page=132', 'p. 132, 159', 'If growers have access to the ascospore maturity model, start fungicide sprays when mature spores are reported by the degree day prediction, otherwise at bud break-green tip'),
	(2068, 1116, 'postharvest hortgro co za pag best practice guidelines for prevention of brusing between harvest and the packh', 'https://postharvest.hortgro.co.za/pag/best-practice-guidelines-for-prevention-of-brusing-between-harvest-and-the-packhouse/', NULL, 'Correct thinning reduces the risk of push-offs. Some plant-growth regulators can also decrease push-offs by stimulating stem elongation in short-stemmed cultivars.'),
	(2069, 1116, 'bctfpg ca horticulture spray thinning growth regulators sun burn protection', 'https://www.bctfpg.ca/horticulture/spray-thinning-growth-regulators-sun-burn-protection/', NULL, 'Accede is a new plant growth regulator that is now registered for apple thinning in Canada. Its active ingredient is a naturally occurring compound, 1-Aminocyclopropane- 1-carboxyllic acid (ACC), the precursor to ethylene synthesis in all plants. Applying Accede when king fruitlets are at the...'),
	(2070, 1056, 'uvm edu orchard fruit treefruit tf horticulture applehortbasics siteselection html', 'https://www.uvm.edu/~orchard/fruit/treefruit/tf_horticulture/AppleHortBasics/SiteSelection.html', NULL, 'Of all the decisions you make in establishing your orchard, choosing the correct site and location has the greatest long-term impact. An orchard is a long-term venture; it may be productive for 30 to 75 years, and in some instances, even longer. It is necessary to make educated and well informed...'),
	(2071, 1056, 'Apples   Botany, Production and Uses   D. Ferree, I. Warrington (CABI, 2003) BBS', '/api/kb/assets/pdf/435dfba709ef04c7/Apples%20-%20Botany%2C%20Production%20and%20Uses%20-%20D.%20Ferree%2C%20I.%20Warrington%20%28CABI%2C%202003%29%20BBS.pdf', NULL, 'In the autumn, the water cools more slowly than the land and thus air masses are warmed as they pass over it. This warmer air delays the onset of early-autumn freezes. This lake effect is of consequence for only a few kilometres from the lake but accounts for the large concentration of orchards...'),
	(2072, 1056, 'bexar tx tamu edu homehort archives of weekly articles davids plant of the week apples for the urban homeowner', 'https://bexar-tx.tamu.edu/homehort/archives-of-weekly-articles-davids-plant-of-the-week/apples-for-the-urban-homeowner/', NULL, 'Apples are a popular homeowner fruit that can be produced successfully in most areas of Texas. For Central/South Texas, the key to producing quality apples in a home orchard are proper and timely care of the trees and variety selection. If you are unwilling to maintain the trees and fruit, then...'),
	(2073, 1064, 'Apples   Botany, Production and Uses   D. Ferree, I. Warrington (CABI, 2003) BBS', '/api/kb/assets/pdf/435dfba709ef04c7/Apples%20-%20Botany%2C%20Production%20and%20Uses%20-%20D.%20Ferree%2C%20I.%20Warrington%20%28CABI%2C%202003%29%20BBS.pdf#page=131', 'p. 131', 'Fly-speck is caused by Schizothyrium pomi (Mont.: Fr.) Arx (anamorph Zygophiala jamaicensis E. Mason). Ascospores of S. pomi, which are produced in thyrothecia on reservoir hosts, provide the primary inoculum for infections. While some infections occur on fruit, the most important infections...'),
	(2074, 1064, 'extension psu edu nematodes preventing problems in deciduous fruit trees', 'https://extension.psu.edu/nematodes-preventing-problems-in-deciduous-fruit-trees/', NULL, 'The symptoms of orchard replant disease include stunting, yellowing of leaves, discolored and necrotic feeder roots, and, in severe cases, tree death within the first few years after planting. Necrotic roots may or may not show obvious lesions. Typically, affected trees show a patchy...'),
	(2075, 1064, 'pnwhandbooks org plantdisease host disease apple malus spp nematode root lesion', 'https://pnwhandbooks.org/plantdisease/host-disease/apple-malus-spp-nematode-root-lesion', NULL, 'MeloCon WG (Paecilomyces lilacinus strain 251) at 2 to 4 lb/A plus a soil wetting agent can be applied to established plants, although it might be better used when applied to plants just before planting. Stable for only days at room temperature, weeks in the refrigerator or for a year if frozen....'),
	(2076, 1105, 'pubs ext vt edu 422 422 023 422 023 html', 'https://www.pubs.ext.vt.edu/422/422-023/422-023.html', NULL, 'At other times trees may be budded high and there may be 10 to 18 inches of rootstock below the bud union. In this case, plant the tree so the highest roots are about 4 inches below the soil. Where visible, the original soil line on the rootstock can be used as a guide for planting depth. If the...'),
	(2077, 1105, 'canr msu edu news planting fruit trees', 'https://www.canr.msu.edu/news/planting_fruit_trees', NULL, 'Scion rooting of apple trees on dwarfing rootstocks is a serious and common problem caused by deep planting. || the unions are not visible and trees appear abnormally vigorous || adventitious roots arising from the scion become dominant'),
	(2078, 1095, 'web archive org web 19981205074522id http www caf wvu edu kearneysville disease descriptions ombitter html', 'https://web.archive.org/web/19981205074522id_/http://www.caf.wvu.edu/kearneysville/disease_descriptions/ombitter.html', NULL, 'Some cultural practices may help > > reduce inoculum and thus reduce the incidence of the disease. Cultural practices > > include removing mummified fruit, dead wood, and fire-blighted twigs from trees and > > removing newly infected fruit during the growing season.'),
	(2079, 1095, 'Penn State Tree Fruit Produc', '/api/kb/assets/pdf/e5ae1a65affc1a1b/Penn_State_Tree_Fruit_Produc.pdf#page=119', 'p. 119, 120, 126', 'Phytophthora collar, crown, and root rots continue to be a major cause of tree death in Pennsylvania orchards. These rots can affect both pome and stone fruit. || The fungus can infect apple trees in the following ways: (1) collar rot, infection above the tree union; (2) crown rot, infection of...'),
	(2080, 1095, 'niab com chemical control apple canker', 'https://www.niab.com/chemical-control-apple-canker', NULL, 'The recent inoculation studies indicate a slight increase in fruit susceptibility to *Neonectria ditissima* pre-harvest, but it is not known whether there is any benefit from additional sprays at this time and there is the risk of fungicide residues in fruit from the late applications.'),
	(2081, 1073, '2020 21 australian apple and pear ipdm manual', '/api/kb/assets/pdf/44a02a4cb9e3415a/2020-21-australian-apple-and-pear-ipdm-manual.pdf#page=93', 'p. 93, 163, 229', '1-minute inspection/tree As you spend one-minute walking around a tree, or along a panel of trellised trees, count and record the number of Budworm (Heliothis), Looper, Pear Slug, Lightbrown Apple Moth (LBAM) larvae, weevils, and mealybugs you see. During the same inspection look for:'),
	(2082, 1073, 'Apple IPM   Obliquebanded Leafroller : Fruit : Center for Agriculture, Food, and the Environment (CA', 'https://www.umass.edu/agriculture-food-environment/fruit/fact-sheets/apple-ipm-obliquebanded-leafroller', NULL, '# Apple IPM - Obliquebanded Leafroller || Injuries occurring early in the season cause pronounced deformations of the fruit and are impossible to differentiate from the damage of green fruitworms. Late season fruit feeding causes small pits in the fruit surface that may go undetected until after...'),
	(2083, 1073, 'canr msu edu ipm diseases tufted apple bud moth', 'https://www.canr.msu.edu/ipm/diseases/tufted_apple_bud_moth', NULL, 'Use pheromone traps and a degree-day developmental model to time insecticide sprays against small larvae starting after the fruit thinning period and again in late summer. || ### Crops Affected: apples, cherries, peaches, pears'),
	(2084, 1061, 'bctfpg ca horticulture spray thinning growth regulators sun burn protection', 'https://www.bctfpg.ca/horticulture/spray-thinning-growth-regulators-sun-burn-protection/', NULL, 'Begin applications once the fruit reach 19 mm, with follow up applications every 2 to 3 weeks. The first application should be made at the high rate, 30 L per hectare (12 L per acre); follow up applications can be made at the lower rate, 20 L per hectare (8 L per acre). **Purshade should be...'),
	(2085, 1090, 'web archive org web 19981205025609id http www caf wvu edu kearneysville disease descriptions omsooty html', 'https://web.archive.org/web/19981205025609id_/http://www.caf.wvu.edu/kearneysville/disease_descriptions/omsooty.html', NULL, 'Sooty blotch and flyspeck > > are surface blemish diseases that commonly appear together on apple or pear in late summer > > and fall. || **Sooty Blotch, *Peltaster fructicola, Geastrumia polystigmatus, Leptodontium elatus*, > > and Flyspeck, *Zygophiala jamaicensis***'),
	(2086, 1090, 'ohioline osu edu factsheet plpath fru 42', 'https://ohioline.osu.edu/factsheet/plpath-fru-42', NULL, 'Apple fruits often become infected from mid-summer on without showing external symptoms. Thus, fruit may be infected without symptoms appearing in the orchard. Disease development is checked when these apples are placed in cold storage. However, when they are removed from cold storage an...'),
	(2087, 1090, 'Apples   Botany, Production and Uses   D. Ferree, I. Warrington (CABI, 2003) BBS', '/api/kb/assets/pdf/435dfba709ef04c7/Apples%20-%20Botany%2C%20Production%20and%20Uses%20-%20D.%20Ferree%2C%20I.%20Warrington%20%28CABI%2C%202003%29%20BBS.pdf#page=131', 'p. 131', 'Fly-speck is caused by Schizothyrium pomi (Mont.: Fr.) Arx (anamorph Zygophiala jamaicensis E. Mason). Ascospores of S. pomi, which are produced in thyrothecia on reservoir hosts, provide the primary inoculum for infections. While some infections occur on fruit, the most important infections...'),
	(2088, 1069, 'Kumawat 2021 Tall Spindle Apple orchard planting system f', '/api/kb/assets/pdf/f9c53384f34ce57e/Kumawat_2021_Tall-Spindle-Apple-orchard-planting-system-f.pdf', NULL, 'This can be achieved by annual removal of large one or two upper branches completely by “bevel cut” so that small stub of the lower portion of branch remains which often result in flat, weak replacement branch. When such type of pruning is repeated annually, the top of the tree can be composed...'),
	(2089, 1069, 'pubs ext vt edu 422 422 023 422 023 html', 'https://www.pubs.ext.vt.edu/422/422-023/422-023.html', NULL, 'The central leader will have 2 to 4 narrow-crotched upright shoots developing just below the previous year’s pruning cut. Retain the longest straightest shoot and remove the top 1/3 of it. Remove all narrow-crotched shoots below the new central leader. Retain all limbs with wide-angled crotches...'),
	(2090, 1071, 'bctfpg ca horticulture fruit tree nutrition essential mineral nutrients in plants deficiency toxicity symptoms', 'https://www.bctfpg.ca/horticulture/fruit-tree-nutrition/essential-mineral-nutrients-in-plants-deficiency-toxicity-symptoms-sources-recommendations/zinc-zn/', NULL, 'For apples, it is recommended that Zn sulphate be applied annually at silver tip to green tip stage of bud development (stages 2 and 3), supplemented by one or more sprays of chelated foliar formulations of Zn during the growing season.'),
	(2091, 1071, 'bctfpg ca horticulture crop management', 'https://www.bctfpg.ca/horticulture/crop-management/', NULL, '• Apply [dormant zinc sulphate spray](https://www.bctfpg.ca/horticulture/fruit-tree-nutrition/essential-mineral-nutrients-in-plants-deficiency-toxicity-symptoms-sources-recommendations/zinc-zn/) (before oil) as required'),
	(2092, 1071, 'Penn State Tree Fruit Produc', '/api/kb/assets/pdf/e5ae1a65affc1a1b/Penn_State_Tree_Fruit_Produc.pdf#page=27', 'p. 27', 'Boron is most effective when applied as a foliar spray on apples and to a lesser extent on pears. || Foliar applications can be made during bloom or postharvest while leaves are still green and active on the tree.'),
	(2093, 1085, 'Bradshaw 2018 Status of IPM Practice Adoption in Vermont Ap', '/api/kb/assets/pdf/7462aac0f0d9e420/Bradshaw_2018_Status-of-IPM-Practice-Adoption-in-Vermont-Ap.pdf', NULL, 'Most growers likely applied a delayed-dormant copper application to reduce overwintering bacterial inoculum, which is strongly recommended by all plant pathologists and IPM specialists in the region (Clements et al. 2015, Cooley et al. 2015).'),
	(2094, 1085, '2023 2024 New Jersey Commercial Tree Fruit Production Guide', '/api/kb/assets/pdf/5769fc173448184d/2023_2024%20New%20Jersey%20Commercial%20Tree%20Fruit%20Production%20Guide.pdf', NULL, NULL),
	(2095, 1085, 'extension uconn edu publication ipm plan san jose scale', 'https://extension.uconn.edu/publication/ipm-plan-san-jose-scale', NULL, 'A dormant or delayed dormant oil application can be applied before pink bud stage to reduce overwintering populations.'),
	(2096, 1092, 'extension psu edu apple disease core rot', 'https://extension.psu.edu/apple-disease-core-rot', NULL, 'Dry core rot is a slow, dry, and corky rot that affects the mesoderm tissue (flesh) surrounding the core. External symptoms are rare, except infected fruit may color and fall prematurely. Wet core rot is a more aggressive wet rot that rapidly develops further during storage and may cause partial...'),
	(2097, 1092, 'Penn State Tree Fruit Produc', '/api/kb/assets/pdf/e5ae1a65affc1a1b/Penn_State_Tree_Fruit_Produc.pdf#page=119', 'p. 119, 120, 126', 'Phytophthora collar, crown, and root rots continue to be a major cause of tree death in Pennsylvania orchards. These rots can affect both pome and stone fruit. || The fungus can infect apple trees in the following ways: (1) collar rot, infection above the tree union; (2) crown rot, infection of...'),
	(2098, 1092, 'CommercialStorage', '/api/kb/assets/pdf/98fe86ba0a133c7d/CommercialStorage.pdf#page=201', 'p. 201', 'Many of the biocontrol agents selected and developed to date have proven very effective in controlled tests, but commercialization of biocontrols has been slow. Product developers view the market potential for postharvest treatments as relatively limited because the products are applied in a...'),
	(2099, 1099, 'treefruit wsu edu orchard management pollination honey bees', 'https://treefruit.wsu.edu/orchard-management/pollination/honey-bees/', NULL, '(*Notes to Class Designations:* \*1. If temperature is below 50°F all day, then it is safe to spray at any time of day. \*2. If temperature is above 50°F, do not spray until after 7 p.m. \*3. If temperature is above 50°F, do not spray until after 7 p.m., and stop spraying at 7 a.m.) || Class...'),
	(2100, 1099, 'bctfpg ca horticulture varieties and pollination', 'https://www.bctfpg.ca/horticulture/varieties-and-pollination/', NULL, '5\. Do not dump unused dusts or sprays where they might become a hazard to bees (and the environment). Bees may sometimes collect any type of fine dust material when pollen is not readily available. Under such conditions, pesticide dusts may be brought back to the colony where the entire...'),
	(2101, 1074, 'niab com chemical control apple canker', 'https://www.niab.com/chemical-control-apple-canker', NULL, 'The recent inoculation studies indicate a slight increase in fruit susceptibility to *Neonectria ditissima* pre-harvest, but it is not known whether there is any benefit from additional sprays at this time and there is the risk of fungicide residues in fruit from the late applications.'),
	(2103, 1058, 'niab com flower blossom thinning', 'https://www.niab.com/flower-blossom-thinning', NULL, 'Other blossom thinners that have shown promise in trials both in the UK and abroad include [Armothin](/node/1899), common [salt (sodium chloride)](/node/1904), [Endothallic acid](/node/1896), [Ethephon](/node/1900), Lime sulphur, [Pelargonic acid](/node/1897), [Urea](/node/1901),...'),
	(2104, 1058, 'pubs ext vt edu content pubs ext vt edu en 422 422 023 422 023 html', 'https://www.pubs.ext.vt.edu/content/pubs_ext_vt_edu/en/422/422-023/422-023.html', NULL, 'Fruits developing from flowers that were not pollinated or fertilized will drop before developing to the 1/2 inch size. More fruit will fall before average fruit diameter is 1 inch, probably due to a lack of carbohydrate in the tree.'),
	(2105, 1058, 'pubs ext vt edu 422 422 023 422 023 html', 'https://www.pubs.ext.vt.edu/422/422-023/422-023.html', NULL, '**Fruit Growers Calendar:** Fruit Production is a Year-Round Activity || | Month | Activity | || | May | * Install rodent guards around trunk of newly planted trees. * Thin fruit with chemicals or by hand. * Apply petal fall and first cover spray. * Remove fireblight strikes. * Discourage deer...'),
	(2106, 1106, 'niab com do i need thin and which method should i use', 'https://www.niab.com/do-i-need-thin-and-which-method-should-i-use', NULL, 'Before deciding on blossom thinning it is important to ask: * Does historical data show consistently that thinning is necessary? * Are the flower cluster numbers twice as high (or more) than necessary for a good set? * Has there been little or no frost damage and none forecast? If the answer is...'),
	(2107, 1106, 'Greene 1983 Effects of Dormant Pruning Summer Pruning Sco', 'https://doi.org/10.21273/jashs.108.4.590', NULL, 'Table 4. Effects of summer pruning, corrective dormant pruning (CDP), scoring, and daminozide on bloom, fruit set, and growth of ‘Red Prince Delicious’ apples, 1978–80. || Terminal growth prior to summer pruning (cm) || CDP + daminozide 1500 ppm + NAA on dormant cuts + summer pruning || 25 c || 1979'),
	(2108, 1106, 'bctfpg ca horticulture spray thinning growth regulators sun burn protection', 'https://www.bctfpg.ca/horticulture/spray-thinning-growth-regulators-sun-burn-protection/', NULL, 'Accede is a new plant growth regulator that is now registered for apple thinning in Canada. Its active ingredient is a naturally occurring compound, 1-Aminocyclopropane- 1-carboxyllic acid (ACC), the precursor to ethylene synthesis in all plants. Applying Accede when king fruitlets are at the...'),
	(2109, 1076, 'bctfpg ca horticulture spray thinning growth regulators sun burn protection', 'https://www.bctfpg.ca/horticulture/spray-thinning-growth-regulators-sun-burn-protection/', NULL, 'Each package of ReTain contains 333 grams of material, or 50 grams active ingredient. The label rate for all apple cultivars is 125 g active ingredient (2.5 packages) per hectare (50 g/acre = 1 package/A) applied with enough water to thoroughly wet the fruit and foliage (about 900 L/ha, 80...'),
	(2110, 1076, 'Arseneault 2016 A review of apple preharvest fruit drop and p', 'https://doi.org/10.1016/j.scienta.2016.08.002', NULL, 'while starch indices of attached fruit were between 5.7 and 7.2 (Poapst et al., 1959). || A 5-year investigation using ‘McIntosh’ apples demonstrated that fruit susceptible to PFD were more advanced in maturity with greater degradation of starch, compared to fruit that remained on the tree...'),
	(2111, 1076, 'Liu 2022 Effects of Aminoethoxyvinylglycine AVG and 1M', 'https://doi.org/10.3390/horticulturae8121100', NULL, 'Stem-end splitting (SES) was evaluated for all fruits harvested two weeks after the normal harvest date (7 September). || No fruit cracking was observed on trees treated with a full-rate of AVG or a half-rate of AVG in conjunction with two applications of 1-MCP. || Table 3. Effects of AVG and...'),
	(2112, 1088, '2023 2024 New Jersey Commercial Tree Fruit Production Guide', '/api/kb/assets/pdf/5769fc173448184d/2023_2024%20New%20Jersey%20Commercial%20Tree%20Fruit%20Production%20Guide.pdf', NULL, NULL),
	(2113, 1103, 'bctfpg ca horticulture crop management', 'https://www.bctfpg.ca/horticulture/crop-management/', NULL, 'or infested with [shothole](https://www.bctfpg.ca/pest_guide/info/58/Shothole_Borer) or [ambrosia beetles](https://www.bctfpg.ca/pest_guide/info/29/Ambrosia_Beetle)'),
	(2114, 1103, 'Apples   Botany, Production and Uses   D. Ferree, I. Warrington (CABI, 2003) BBS', '/api/kb/assets/pdf/435dfba709ef04c7/Apples%20-%20Botany%2C%20Production%20and%20Uses%20-%20D.%20Ferree%2C%20I.%20Warrington%20%28CABI%2C%202003%29%20BBS.pdf#page=334', 'p. 334, 345, 373', 'Cultivars of this type tend to bear early, with most of the fruit on spurs or terminals of short shoots borne on 2- to 4-year-old wood. The fruiting zone on cultivars in this classification tends to move away from the trunk to the outside of the canopy. This requires thinning on the canopy...'),
	(2115, 1103, 'pubs ext vt edu content pubs ext vt edu en 422 422 023 422 023 html', 'https://www.pubs.ext.vt.edu/content/pubs_ext_vt_edu/en/422/422-023/422-023.html', NULL, 'Upright growing branches should be reoriented to 45 to 60° from horizontal. Branches can be spread by placing stiff pieces of wire or wooden sticks between the trunk and upper surface of the branch. Branches can also be spread by tying the branch down with string or hanging weights on the ends...'),
	(2116, 1060, 'bexar tx tamu edu homehort archives of weekly articles davids plant of the week apples for the urban homeowner', 'https://bexar-tx.tamu.edu/homehort/archives-of-weekly-articles-davids-plant-of-the-week/apples-for-the-urban-homeowner/', NULL, 'In areas with alkaline soils, cotton root rot is a severe problem for which there is no control at this time. If your landscape has a history of losing plants to this organism, avoid planting apples because they are very sensitive to it.'),
	(2117, 1060, 'hort extension wisc edu articles dead mans fingers', 'https://hort.extension.wisc.edu/articles/dead-mans-fingers/', NULL, 'Contact the [UW Plant Disease Diagnostics Clinic (PDDC)](https://pddc.wisc.edu/sample-collection-and-submission-2/), and for a small fee, clinic staff can examine a plant, determine the cause of the disease/disorder, and provide advice on how to control or prevent the issue.'),
	(2118, 1060, 'Apples   Botany, Production and Uses   D. Ferree, I. Warrington (CABI, 2003) BBS', '/api/kb/assets/pdf/435dfba709ef04c7/Apples%20-%20Botany%2C%20Production%20and%20Uses%20-%20D.%20Ferree%2C%20I.%20Warrington%20%28CABI%2C%202003%29%20BBS.pdf#page=131', 'p. 131', 'Fly-speck is caused by Schizothyrium pomi (Mont.: Fr.) Arx (anamorph Zygophiala jamaicensis E. Mason). Ascospores of S. pomi, which are produced in thyrothecia on reservoir hosts, provide the primary inoculum for infections. While some infections occur on fruit, the most important infections...'),
	(2119, 1083, 'ohioline osu edu factsheet plpath fru 42', 'https://ohioline.osu.edu/factsheet/plpath-fru-42', NULL, 'Apple fruits often become infected from mid-summer on without showing external symptoms. Thus, fruit may be infected without symptoms appearing in the orchard. Disease development is checked when these apples are placed in cold storage. However, when they are removed from cold storage an...'),
	(2139, 1057, 'blogs cornell edu applevarietydatabase fact sheet white rot', 'https://blogs.cornell.edu/applevarietydatabase/fact-sheet-white-rot', NULL, '- Remove pruned limbs from the orchard completely. Do not leave at the border of the orchard, as they can act as a source of inoculum during the growing season'),
	(2120, 1083, 'web archive org web 19981207070659id http www caf wvu edu kearneysville disease descriptions omapscab html', 'https://web.archive.org/web/19981207070659id_/http://www.caf.wvu.edu/kearneysville/disease_descriptions/omapscab.html', NULL, 'The selection of fungicdes for management of scab is based on several || factors, including the entire spectrum of other diseases that must be managed at that || time, the potential for resistance in the scab fungus to the selected chemical, the || history of the disease in a particular orchard,...'),
	(2121, 1083, 'Penn State Tree Fruit Produc', '/api/kb/assets/pdf/e5ae1a65affc1a1b/Penn_State_Tree_Fruit_Produc.pdf#page=119', 'p. 119, 120, 126', 'Phytophthora collar, crown, and root rots continue to be a major cause of tree death in Pennsylvania orchards. These rots can affect both pome and stone fruit. || The fungus can infect apple trees in the following ways: (1) collar rot, infection above the tree union; (2) crown rot, infection of...'),
	(2122, 1087, 'niab com suitable pollinating varieties', 'https://www.niab.com/suitable-pollinating-varieties', NULL, 'Even in apparently incompatible combinations fruit set is often able to occur. * For instance, trials have shown that when Fiesta received pollen of another variety, with which it should be incompatible, it was able to set a reasonable crop of fruits. * However, when the reciprocal cross was...'),
	(2123, 1087, 'niab com pollen compatibility', 'https://www.niab.com/pollen-compatibility', NULL, 'Early work ([Kobel *et al.* 1939](/node/1827)) showed that by making various possible cross pollinations and observing the speed of pollen tube growth down the style it was possible to distinguish between compatible, semi-compatible (partially compatible) and incompatible crosses.'),
	(2124, 1087, 'extension psu edu orchard pollination pollinizers pollinators and weather', 'https://extension.psu.edu/orchard-pollination-pollinizers-pollinators-and-weather', NULL, 'Growers should exercise caution, however, in selecting a particular crabapple for their orchards. Not all crabapples are suitable for use as pollinizers. Research has shown that white single-flowering crabs are better for cross-pollination because these flowers are most like apple flowers....'),
	(2125, 1102, 'bctfpg ca horticulture spray thinning growth regulators sun burn protection', 'https://www.bctfpg.ca/horticulture/spray-thinning-growth-regulators-sun-burn-protection/', NULL, 'Accede is a new plant growth regulator that is now registered for apple thinning in Canada. Its active ingredient is a naturally occurring compound, 1-Aminocyclopropane- 1-carboxyllic acid (ACC), the precursor to ethylene synthesis in all plants. Applying Accede when king fruitlets are at the...'),
	(2126, 1079, 'bctfpg ca horticulture fruit tree nutrition assessing nutrient requirements in fruit trees sampling testing an', 'https://www.bctfpg.ca/horticulture/fruit-tree-nutrition/assessing-nutrient-requirements-in-fruit-trees-sampling-testing-and-interpretation/fruit-and-fruitlet-analysis/', NULL, 'Fallahi et al. (2010) report that fruit analysis alone or with leaf tissue analysis was useful in making models to predict fruit quality. From models, Ca and N in only fruit could be used to predict bitter pit in apples. Monitoring Ca and N as well as P and K within a year as well as between...'),
	(2127, 1079, 'Arseneault 2016 A review of apple preharvest fruit drop and p', 'https://doi.org/10.1016/j.scienta.2016.08.002', NULL, 'Furthermore, foliar boron sprays applied during rapid fruit growth on the two || cultivars ‘Fuji’ and ‘Orin’ improved fruit soluble sugars and starch at three orchards (Lu et al., 2013).'),
	(2128, 1079, 'apal org au improved calcium absorption for fruit quality', 'https://apal.org.au/improved-calcium-absorption-for-fruit-quality/', NULL, 'Multiple sprays of a mixture of 1 per cent potassium nitrate and calcium nitrate substantially increased foliar calcium levels as well as fruit firmness at harvest. || For these trials, the treatments – using the soluble nitrate forms of potassium and calcium (Table 1) – were applied 20 days...'),
	(2129, 1082, 'bctfpg ca horticulture crop management', 'https://www.bctfpg.ca/horticulture/crop-management/', NULL, '• Avoid mowing blooming ground covers 1 week before bloom until after petal fall (See [western flower thrips](https://www.bctfpg.ca/pest_guide/info/60/Western_Flower_Thrips))'),
	(2130, 1082, '2023 2024 New Jersey Commercial Tree Fruit Production Guide', '/api/kb/assets/pdf/5769fc173448184d/2023_2024%20New%20Jersey%20Commercial%20Tree%20Fruit%20Production%20Guide.pdf', NULL, NULL),
	(2131, 1082, 'Penn State Tree Fruit Produc', '/api/kb/assets/pdf/e5ae1a65affc1a1b/Penn_State_Tree_Fruit_Produc.pdf#page=17', 'p. 17', 'Herbicides must (1) adequately contact the target weeds, (2) be absorbed by the weed, (3) move within the weed to the site of action without being neutralized, and (4) be in high enough concentration to be toxic at the site of action. The mode of action refers to the chain of events from...'),
	(2132, 1053, 'Penn State Tree Fruit Produc', '/api/kb/assets/pdf/e5ae1a65affc1a1b/Penn_State_Tree_Fruit_Produc.pdf#page=17', 'p. 17', 'Herbicides must (1) adequately contact the target weeds, (2) be absorbed by the weed, (3) move within the weed to the site of action without being neutralized, and (4) be in high enough concentration to be toxic at the site of action. The mode of action refers to the chain of events from...'),
	(2133, 1053, '2023 2024 New Jersey Commercial Tree Fruit Production Guide', '/api/kb/assets/pdf/5769fc173448184d/2023_2024%20New%20Jersey%20Commercial%20Tree%20Fruit%20Production%20Guide.pdf', NULL, NULL),
	(2134, 1053, 'omafra gov on ca neworchard english apples 5prepare html', 'https://www.omafra.gov.on.ca/neworchard/english/apples/5prepare.html', NULL, 'If desired, sod can be established in the previous year and rows burnt out with glyphosate or flaming - ensure a weed-free strip at least 1.5m wide to avoid competition from the sod.'),
	(2135, 1101, 'Penn State Tree Fruit Produc', '/api/kb/assets/pdf/e5ae1a65affc1a1b/Penn_State_Tree_Fruit_Produc.pdf#page=119', 'p. 119, 120, 126', 'Phytophthora collar, crown, and root rots continue to be a major cause of tree death in Pennsylvania orchards. These rots can affect both pome and stone fruit. || The fungus can infect apple trees in the following ways: (1) collar rot, infection above the tree union; (2) crown rot, infection of...'),
	(2136, 1101, 'niab com chemical control apple canker', 'https://www.niab.com/chemical-control-apple-canker', NULL, 'The recent inoculation studies indicate a slight increase in fruit susceptibility to *Neonectria ditissima* pre-harvest, but it is not known whether there is any benefit from additional sprays at this time and there is the risk of fungicide residues in fruit from the late applications.'),
	(2137, 1101, 'web archive org web 19990222094526id http www caf wvu edu kearneysville disease descriptions omaund html', 'https://web.archive.org/web/19990222094526id_/http://www.caf.wvu.edu/kearneysville/disease_descriptions/omaund.html', NULL, 'Symptom severity is influenced by scion/rootstock combination; > > ''Delicious'' on MM. 106 rootstock produces extreme symptoms when infected, while ''Golden > > Delicious'', ''Empire'' and ''York'' seldom show symptoms even when the rootstock is infected > > with TMRSV.'),
	(2138, 1057, 'CA Manual Revised', '/api/kb/assets/pdf/dac8958cf8856eca/CA-Manual-Revised.pdf#page=82', 'p. 82, 83, 84', 'Small, brown lesions rapidly increase in size and the fruit is completely decayed within two days. The skin of a decayed fruit has a parchment-like texture and does not break easily. Decayed tissue is very watery. Spores are produced at skin breaks and at the stem and calyx ends of the affected...'),
	(2140, 1057, 'ohioline osu edu factsheet plpath fru 42', 'https://ohioline.osu.edu/factsheet/plpath-fru-42', NULL, 'Apple fruits often become infected from mid-summer on without showing external symptoms. Thus, fruit may be infected without symptoms appearing in the orchard. Disease development is checked when these apples are placed in cold storage. However, when they are removed from cold storage an...'),
	(2141, 1114, 'web archive org web 19981207070659id http www caf wvu edu kearneysville disease descriptions omapscab html', 'https://web.archive.org/web/19981207070659id_/http://www.caf.wvu.edu/kearneysville/disease_descriptions/omapscab.html', NULL, 'The selection of fungicdes for management of scab is based on several || factors, including the entire spectrum of other diseases that must be managed at that || time, the potential for resistance in the scab fungus to the selected chemical, the || history of the disease in a particular orchard,...'),
	(2142, 1114, 'Penn State Tree Fruit Produc', '/api/kb/assets/pdf/e5ae1a65affc1a1b/Penn_State_Tree_Fruit_Produc.pdf#page=119', 'p. 119, 120, 126', 'Phytophthora collar, crown, and root rots continue to be a major cause of tree death in Pennsylvania orchards. These rots can affect both pome and stone fruit. || The fungus can infect apple trees in the following ways: (1) collar rot, infection above the tree union; (2) crown rot, infection of...'),
	(2143, 1070, 'Wang 2016 LongTerm Application of Bioorganic Fertilizer', 'https://doi.org/10.3389/fmicb.2016.01893', NULL, NULL),
	(2144, 1070, 'treefruit wsu edu fall nutrient sprays in tree fruit', 'https://treefruit.wsu.edu/fall-nutrient-sprays-in-tree-fruit', NULL, 'In the PNW, deficiencies are most frequently in soils that are cold, wet, sandy and alkaline (pH above 7.5) where Zn becomes unavailable. Under these conditions, the deficiency relates more to a lack of uptake rather than a lack of supply; therefore, soil application of Zn is inefficient.'),
	(2145, 1070, 'bctfpg ca horticulture fruit tree nutrition essential mineral nutrients in plants deficiency toxicity symptoms', 'https://www.bctfpg.ca/horticulture/fruit-tree-nutrition/essential-mineral-nutrients-in-plants-deficiency-toxicity-symptoms-sources-recommendations/zinc-zn/', NULL, 'For apples, it is recommended that Zn sulphate be applied annually at silver tip to green tip stage of bud development (stages 2 and 3), supplemented by one or more sprays of chelated foliar formulations of Zn during the growing season.');
